./logs/iter_006_synthesis.stderr.log:1742:For finite \(m\), write the tail masses as \(S_i=\Pr(C\ge c_i)\). Equal revenue imposes \(c_iS_i=R\). If \(S_1=1\), \(S_m=R\), and ratios \(S_{i+1}/S_i\) are all equal to \(r=(m-1)/m\), then the gap becomes \(r^m\). AM-GM gives the expected upper bound once one proves the optimizer can be made equal-revenue with top atom at \(1\).
