./logs/iter_009_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:770:The finite multi-continuation terminal-block lift is also accepted for universal/process-unaware lower bounds: for a common zero block and finite threshold set \(C\), some deterministic continuation has regret at least \(N\kappa(C)-M\), where \(M\) caps old rewards. Choosing \(m\)-point equal-revenue menus and diagonalizing \(m\to\infty\) gives a universal terminal-block lower-bound constant approaching \(1/e\). This still does not imply an instance-wise tail characterization.
