./logs/iter_009_synthesis.stderr.log:8343: Iteration 7 sharpens the internal threshold geometry: the exact \(m\)-positive-support local gap is \(((m-1)/m)^m\), approaching \(1/e\). The new price-discrimination/robust-pricing sources above are useful context for equal-revenue and minimax duality, but the finite-support constant and the terminal-block \(1/e\) universal lift should currently be cited as internal results, not as imported theorems.
./logs/iter_009_synthesis.stderr.log:8347:+Iteration 9 adds two internal results: the exact finite-\(C\) local root formula \(\kappa(C)=\delta_*(C)\), and the universal equal-revenue \(1/e\) upper bound for exogenous horizon-oblivious paths. A narrow literature check found robust/minimax-pricing analogies but no direct source for the exact root formula or the delayed-market-making \(1/e\) theorem. Treat Bergemann-Schlag 2011 and Caldentey-Liu-Lobel 2017 as adjacent context only, and Anagnostides et al. 2026 as a weak approachability analogy only.
./logs/iter_009_synthesis.stderr.log:8354: Iteration 8 verifies the equal-revenue primal certificate for a single block: uniform mass on quotes just below the equal-revenue thresholds gives constant local deficit \(((m-1)/m)^m\), matching the dual \(\kappa(C)\). For arbitrary finite \(C\), the primal optimizer and any compositional known-path upper bound remain open.
./logs/iter_009_synthesis.stderr.log:8376:+The upper bound is the universal equal-revenue quote law \(d\mu(a)=a^{-1}1\{e^{-1}\le a\le1\}\,da\); the lower bound is CL-027. Next steps:
